{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/318724-how-powerful-should-this-dragonblood-be","id":318724,"title":"How powerful should this Dragonblood be?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-21T22:27:53-08:00","id":318724,"title":"How powerful should this Dragonblood be?","content":"I'm running a game where a character has a dragonblooded sibling (ally 3). But not sure how strong he should be. He's been exalted for almost 20 years and basically works as Lookshy Black Ops. I am thinking essence 4 or 5. Not really sure how much experience to give him though. I wanted opinions I dont have alot of experience with terrestrials","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T22:45:44-08:00","id":318759,"title":"","content":"essence 5 may be a bit much for being only 20 years exalted, if i recall dragonblooded dont tend to raise their essence very fast and it takes some time (And a fair amount of XP to do so)...the Dragonblooded book in the experience section states that average, say a dragonblooded that exalted at 15, and is 100 years old, based on the normal experience scale they would have about 850 XP. So divide that by 5 (to put it at a 20 year age) you have about 170, though for an NPC that seems a bit much. However it really depends on what you are planning to use this ally for the powerlevel of your game etc.<br /> <br /> There is also a handy XP table in the core book that shows how much XP you should get over a certain amount of time. (I'd look it up but i dont know where my core book ran off to)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T00:56:41-08:00","id":318787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeroz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/318724-how-powerful-should-this-dragonblood-be#post318724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm running a game where a character has a dragonblooded sibling (ally 3). But not sure how strong he should be. He's been exalted for almost 20 years and basically works as Lookshy Black Ops. I am thinking essence 4 or 5. Not really sure how much experience to give him though. I wanted opinions I dont have alot of experience with terrestrials</div> </div> </div> </div>Essence 5 is pushing it, that puts you on the verge of elder exalt territory. I would personally go for essence 3, a DB who has only been exalted for 20 years is still a baby in comparison to his parents, or heck older siblings for that matter. If you want him to be a skilled operative, I would go ahead and bump his abilities up a bit, or give him a wider array of tactically useful charms from across the different trees. Essence 4 is probably on the edge of what I would exspect, if you do go to 4, I would make it so that he had just hit that mark, and limit the charms you give him at that level to a couple if not just one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","user":"turkeygiant","date":". 11-22-2014, 04:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T02:59:15-08:00","id":318833,"title":"","content":"I'd go for Essence 3, because he's an Ally 3.<br /> It doesn't really matter about his XP compared to his age, that's just background, (he could be a very active or very inactive guy, after all) just that he's got the right amount of XP for an Ally 3.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T03:38:06-08:00","id":318844,"title":"","content":"Essence 3 sounds reasonable. 20 years as an Exalt is a fledgling, even as a Terrestrial. Remember they can live to be 300+ years old. I say build the character as a starting Dragon Blood then assign about 40xp spread reasonably around the character based on their activities during their 20 years as an exalt. Remember that at least 5 or so of those years are likely to have been spent in a Secondary school of some kind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","name":"NuSoardGraphite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T07:28:53-08:00","id":318961,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind that each dot of Allies usually represents 1 ally at approximately starting character strength. More powerful allies cost more. They also are supposed to have lives of their own and won't necessarily follow the character around or sacrifice themselves for their brother.a<br /> <br /> So under these guidelines, I would recommend this approach: <br /> <br /> 1) Decide how the 3-dot ally is going to be useful to the player character. This should be done with the help of the player. Make sure he's not just using his ally as a cheap way to get more artifacts through the arsenal or artifact backgrounds. I would say give him one area of expertise per dot of background. So in this instance, 3 areas of expertise.<br /> 2) Stat out a starting character.<br /> 3) Add bonus points/XP as necessary for purchases of traits/charms/backgrounds that make the Ally worth 3-dots to your character.<br /> <br /> A personal recommendation is that you don't use personal combat as the way to distinguish this guy as a 3-dot ally. Sure he can probably be a great fighter, he is in the special forces after all. But I would give him several areas of expertise outside of fighting that make him useful and keep him from following the PC around at all times. My recommendation is that he have access to an intelligence network, lots of connections in the scavenger lands that allow him to get the PC audiences with high ranking officials in various city states, and perhaps command of a small strike force which, although not at the PCs disposal, could be brought in to assist with major threats like a boss fight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1g_IC644YJoiVAm6ngqcBmsQtff2YYtd3pDbZpaOxx4o\" target=\"_blank\">My Exalted Character Creation Tool may be downloaded here.</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1086797-demac-s-exalted-character-creation-tool\" target=\"_blank\">The thread talking about the tool can be found here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1136654-exalted-seats-of-power\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted: Seats of Power is a homebrewed manse creation system.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1oaq3wk7lJKZ022SUA4iPfGzMpmBTNXlM\" target=\"_blank\">I have a rewrite of the craft system which can be downloaded here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1070312-i-got-my-book-it-s-super-fancy-and-i-can-t-read-the-cover/page2\" target=\"_blank\">I like the Mesoamerican look</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2346-demac","name":"Demac","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T09:55:25-08:00","id":319998,"title":"","content":"I tend to use the allies ratings in lords of creation as a guideline. If the player taking the allies is a non celestial I tend to make them 1-2 points lower as allies 1 is a starting character of your type in my games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1166-korekore","name":"korekore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1166_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T14:32:01-08:00","id":320194,"title":"","content":"note, Ive got the impression that Theirs no law saying that an elder charachter <i>has</i> to be powersful it noted someplace that plenty of elder exalts, out of lazyness, or fear at some of the inner contradictions they might encounter if they took the break to meditate, or are so overworked they never have the time.<br /> <br /> Point is theirs plenty of centuries old exalts without transhuman essence.<br /> <br /> Your 20 years exalted char could be Essence 2 or 3 or 4, whatever you think is best for the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T11:30:26-08:00","id":320906,"title":"","content":"Well, an Ally 1 is supposed to be roughly as powerful as a starting character in your campaign. An Ally 3 is supposed to be significantly above that. A rating 4 is something as powerful as the Harvester of Poisons, and that's pretty mighty. If you are playing a Solar game, a strong Essence 3 Dragon-Blood is probably good. Maybe 100 xp or so? It will vary on your game. You want someone who is stronger than a starting character in your game, but someone who won't overshadow the PCs, and taht's tricky. Also, what role does your player want this Ally to fill?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T11:57:02-08:00","id":320963,"title":"","content":"I'm the player with the Ally 3 Dragonblooded in Aeroz's game. <br /> <br /> This Ally is my character's older brother. I want the Ally to give my character an emotional connection to something in Creation. As I explained to Aeroz, my character might have a Dragon Blooded Ally, but my character is on her brother's character sheet as an Solar Ally. <br /> <br /> I haven't really considered power level of the character all that much when I put three dots in the background. I told Aeroz that the DB was Water Aspected and a spy type character. I wanted the DB to have his own things to do and not follow the PC party around. I tried to work the background where if the ST needs to introduce plot, he can use my DB ally. <br /> <br /> The DB isn't all that old compared to other Dragon blooded, so I figured he would have a information network worthy of a 3-point ally. However, I am not going to complain if he ends up being a high essence DB. Heck, I makes sense as a Starting Solar character that her older brother would be more powerful. But eventually, I would like there be a moment where balance of power in the relationship flips. Right now, the DB sees my character as someone to protect. After a time, my character will see her older brother as someone she needs to protect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T12:24:42-08:00","id":320996,"title":"","content":"Makes sense. So, the starting ground is a Solar game, using normal character creation rules? I think Essence 3, with about 100 xp is about right, though I would throw some more background dots into the equation. I would also split that 100 xp into 1/3 combat, 1/3 social, and 1/3 stealth/larceny. That will give him a wide range of Abilities, and he won't overpower anything. 100 xp is quite a bit, and turns him into a very powerful character early, and should stay on par with your character for a while. (No-one jump in with the argument that starting Solar should kill a 100 xp DB, please. I'm talking about what the character can accomplish in acting as an ally, not as a bodyshield.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T17:05:04-08:00","id":321186,"title":"","content":"Part of the problem with the Ally background is that at best it only can give a vague measurement of the mechanical strength of an NPC, as opposed to the level of functionality/capability of that character.<br /> <br /> An Essence 5 Lunar who spends most of it's time in the shape of a house cat and sleeping is not going to rate very highly on the scale. On the other hand a competent essence 3 ghost-blooded necromancer with the right skills and methods can easily rank Ally 4 or 5.<br /> <br /> Also I have one random question, as a PC gains in power, do people actively adjust their Backgrounds during the games? By this I mean back when you are an Essence 2 starting character, what Is classified as say a 3 dot Ally will be a very different critter compared to when the same character is an Essence 7 power house.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T19:15:17-08:00","id":321286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/318724-how-powerful-should-this-dragonblood-be?p=320194#post320194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">note, Ive got the impression that Theirs no law saying that an elder charachter <i>has</i> to be powersful it noted someplace that plenty of elder exalts, out of lazyness, or fear at some of the inner contradictions they might encounter if they took the break to meditate, or are so overworked they never have the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>*nods* Dynasts outside the Immaculate Order for example do not generally have the luxury to put their political machinations and business of their House on hold for long enough for the essence-refining meditations and exercises required to raise their essence particularly high. Same goes for DB soldiers in the Legions of the Realm or Lookshy. Of course there are exceptions. You can reasonable put your character's essence wherever your story needs it to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T19:44:42-08:00","id":321320,"title":"","content":"I explored recently a group of outcastes, and a godblooded and mountainfolk Keeping watch in plenilune, while Ranneth was off raising his essence.<br /> <br /> Nobles seeking to retake power became bolder, A small yozi cult sprung into existence, and a GSP tried to kill one of the PC's.<br /> <br /> I mentioned this elsewhere but the point that was made on the players is that who knows what could happen while your off seeking enlightenment.<br /> <br /> And you have to try not to even THINK about it.<br /> <br /> Just think, what it will look like, when Ocean Pearl, Admiral Sand, The Bull of the North, or Dace try to raise their essence.<br /> <br /> Ocean Pearls the Captain of a Pirateship, whats she do tell them &quot;Take 3 months shore leave&quot;<br /> <br /> Admiral Sand will have to leave the fate of his growing merchant empire to Fate, letting enterprising guildsmen do who knows what while hes gone...<br /> <br /> Kaneko could see rebellion throughout his empire that bound demons, Tribal champions and allys go hither and thither suppressing, if not another realm invasion.<br /> <br /> Dace might see the same possiblety as Ocean pearl &quot;Take 3 months of furlough, you've earned it men!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 11-24-2014, 10:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T13:37:11-08:00","id":322119,"title":"","content":"The notion of having to wander into the wilderness and leave the group and personal responsibilities behind to improve yourself is well-steeped in myth but truly terrible in practice when playing a game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T14:35:26-08:00","id":322209,"title":"","content":"but ideas of what you can do if you command a military force, caravan, city, whatever?<br /> <br /> (You dont think thats a mean thing to make my players explore do you?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T14:46:23-08:00","id":322212,"title":"","content":"I would the eliminate the mandatory Buddhist ascetic meditation aspect that really derails games when either one person goes off and the game goes on without him, or the party is split and he has desert adventures, or the whole party goes off at the same time and leaves things behind.<br /> <br /> Simply, I'd let them treat time acting within their Caste roles as time training to raise Essence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T14:46:26-08:00","id":322213,"title":"","content":"I imagine from developer comments that Essence development will be a more &quot;learning on the job&quot; kind of thing from herein.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T15:01:54-08:00","id":322220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/318724-how-powerful-should-this-dragonblood-be?p=322213#post322213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine from developer comments that Essence development will be a more &quot;learning on the job&quot; kind of thing from herein.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T15:32:36-08:00","id":322235,"title":"","content":"Much as I'm seldom ga-ga about furthering a derail,* wasn't there some rule about spontaneously raising one's Essence rating under a particular circumstance? Possibly completing one's Motivation (provided said Motivation was &quot;epic enough,&quot; to use the phrasing I recall)? If I'm not just imagining it, I wonder if some spiritual successor to the idea will carry on into the next edition.<br /> <br /> * Odd, as I seem to do it every other post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T15:48:25-08:00","id":322241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/318724-how-powerful-should-this-dragonblood-be?p=322235#post322235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Much as I'm seldom ga-ga about furthering a derail,* wasn't there some rule about spontaneously raising one's Essence rating under a particular circumstance? Possibly completing one's Motivation (provided said Motivation was &quot;epic enough,&quot; to use the phrasing I recall)? If I'm not just imagining it, I wonder if some spiritual successor to the idea will carry on into the next edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, if you have the XP, fulfilling Motivation lets you raise Essence immediately as a Moment of Awesome (problem: gaming the Motivation to be a relatively easy win condition). And IIRC going from 2 to 3 has no training time either. <br /> <br /> I wonder how that would work with no Motivation and Defining Intimacies not being &quot;goal conditions.&quot; But merely counting &quot;acting in Caste role&quot; as training time is a house rule I use and probably will continue to if the nonsensical training time stuff continues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T17:19:45-08:00","id":322274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/318724-how-powerful-should-this-dragonblood-be?p=322241#post322241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, if you have the XP, fulfilling Motivation lets you raise Essence immediately as a Moment of Awesome (problem: gaming the Motivation to be a relatively easy win condition). And IIRC going from 2 to 3 has no training time either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, good. Thanks. That was about what I remembered. The concerns of gaming it were about what I remembered, too. :/ If it's most appropriate for your character to have a Motivation that by its nature has no real end or almost certainly won't reach it by game's end? Wellp, guess your easy development options are capped.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I wonder how that would work with no Motivation and Defining Intimacies not being &quot;goal conditions.&quot; But merely counting &quot;acting in Caste role&quot; as training time is a house rule I use and probably will continue to if the nonsensical training time stuff continues. </div> </div> </div>I definitely wasn't thinking of anything so direct as completing a goal condition. While I really liked the idea of spontaneously being able to buy up an Essence level at a dramatic moment, the implementation put me off, as above. Honestly, I could be satisfied with not hard-coding it into something so mechanical: if it's a scene the ST and player(s) agree is sufficiently appropriate in dramatics, tone, etc. then the player may spontaneously buy Essence up (other qualifiers, such as resonance with a Defining Intimacy, some aspect of splat/Caste, and/or clear character growth, may also apply*). Dunno if it would be best for something like it to be published or kept in homebrew, though. &gt;_&gt; I just enjoy the shounen trope of sufficiently dramatic moments with deep personal significance helping to unlock new vistas of power.<br /> <br /> * I'm reminded of this, come to think of it. I didn't think of it at the time (it was in the context of martial artists). but I wonder if John's use of &quot;stats&quot; included Intimacies, here. I don't think it likely, but hey, gotta love rampant speculation (unless you don't).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Essentially, I realized that I did not want players to feel as if their characters had slowed to a crawl, so I began to design and implement a system of bonus XP (codename: Solar XP) that players could earn through specific kinds of roleplaying in line with their character, <b>as established by their stats as well as their castes</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T17:33:37-08:00","id":322279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/318724-how-powerful-should-this-dragonblood-be?p=322274#post322274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* I'm reminded of this, come to think of it. I didn't think of it at the time (it was in the context of martial artists). but I wonder if John's use of &quot;stats&quot; included Intimacies, here. I don't think it likely, but hey, gotta love rampant speculation (unless you don't).</div> </div> </div> </div>Doing cool stuff tied to the things you care about should absolutely be a trigger for getting Solar XP. Moreso than mechanical stats imo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T17:46:39-08:00","id":322282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/318724-how-powerful-should-this-dragonblood-be?p=322279#post322279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doing cool stuff tied to the things you care about should absolutely be a trigger for getting Solar XP. Moreso than mechanical stats imo.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I definitely agree. At least without having seen the social influence and Solar XP systems; could be I'm satisfied with the shape of things. It wouldn't surprise me if the idea ultimately worked this way, the context of that quote just didn't point to it in particular. Even if it doesn't, it's not like it would be hard to houserule in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}